# Output Format Rule

## Artifact Standards
- Generate structured artifacts in Markdown or JSON only.
- Keep sections deterministic and stable across regenerations.
- Include version, status, and traceable references where relevant.

## Documentation Standards
- Use clear headings and concise bullets.
- Avoid ambiguous language and hidden assumptions.
- Keep terminology consistent with PRD and acceptance criteria.

## Schema Discipline
- Prefer typed structured output over free-form prose.
- Validate generated payloads against Zod-aligned schemas.
- On schema failure, return explicit error context and retry path.

## Handoff Package Standard
Required package includes:
- `project-spec/00-brief.md`
- `project-spec/01-clarifications.md`
- `project-spec/02-prd.md`
- `project-spec/03-scope.md`
- `project-spec/04-user-stories.md`
- `project-spec/05-acceptance-criteria.md`
- `project-spec/06-design-map.json`
- `project-spec/07-implementation-plan.md`
- `project-spec/08-test-plan.md`
- `project-spec/09-done-definition.md`
- `project-spec/10-tasks.json`
- `.cursor/rules/001-project-context.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/002-architecture.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/003-task-execution.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/004-design-sync.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/005-output-format.mdc`

## Export Guard
- Export is allowed only after review/approve status is confirmed.
- Block export if critical quality gates are not satisfied.
